**Given:**

Radius of first circle (r) = r

Radius of second circle (R) = 4r

**Formula used:**

Length of direct common tangent = sqrt{(d² - (r₁ - r₂)²)}

Where, d = distance between the centers = r₁ + r₂ (since they touch externally)

**Calculation:**

d = r + 4r = 5r

{Length of direct common tangent} = sqrt{(d² - (r₁ - r₂)²)}

⇒ sqrt{(5r)² - (4r - r)²}

⇒ sqrt{25r² - 9r²}

⇒ sqrt{16r²}

⇒ 4r

**∴ The correct answer is option (3).**
